dashma bundled offline icon pack
================================

This directory holds a small set of generic, self-contained icons that ship with
dashma so the dashboard never needs an internet connection to display a tile icon.

Why this exists
---------------
The favicon proxy (GET /api/favicon) normally fetches icons from remote CDNs
(selfh.st, Google s2, allesedv, duckduckgo, simple icons). In an offline / air-gapped
environment every one of those fails. To stay offline-first, the proxy:

  1. First checks this directory for a file whose base name matches the link's
     app-name variants (see getAppNameVariants() in src/server/routes.js).
  2. Falls back to the remote CDNs when online and no local match is found.
  3. If everything fails, serves default.svg with HTTP 200 (no Google redirect),
     so a tile always shows an icon.

The front-end (src/public/js/main.js) also points its <img onerror> fallback at
/icons/default.svg, so broken or offline icons degrade to the generic icon instead
of disappearing.

Files
-----
  default.svg  - neutral generic link icon (the guaranteed fallback). Do not remove.
  globe.svg    - generic web / internet
  link.svg     - generic hyperlink
  server.svg   - generic server / self-hosted service
  folder.svg   - generic folder / file store
  app.svg      - generic application / app grid

All icons here are simple, hand-authored SVGs (no copyrighted brand logos) and are
released under the same license as dashma.

Adding more icons
-----------------
Drop additional image files (.svg/.png/.jpg/.gif/.webp/.ico) into this directory.
Name the file after the app so it matches automatically: the proxy lower-cases the
link title, strips non-alphanumerics, and tries the no-hyphen slug, the hyphen slug,
and the first word. Examples:

  Title "Portainer"        -> portainer.svg
  Title "Arctic Wolf"      -> arcticwolf.svg (also matches arctic-wolf / arctic)
  Title "SFTP-GO"          -> sftpgo.svg (also matches sftp-go / sftp)

These files are committed to the repo (unlike src/public/uploads/, which is ignored).
Keep the pack lightweight - do not scrape thousands of brand logos.
